 the preview, and sets the cookies described above.", "The Internet Archive (archive.org) streams LibriVox recordings and audio clips. Termly (app.termly.io) serves the consent banner.", "When you pay, you go to Stripe's own checkout page, where Stripe sets its own cookies under its privacy policy. We never see your card details.", "OpenDyslexic, the reading font, is part of the app itself, so choosing it sends nothing to anyone."]}, {"heading": "Do my choices apply on all my devices?", "paragraphs": ["No. Cookie settings you make in your browser, and anything you clear there, apply to that browser on that device only. You'll need to make them again on a different device or browser, and a private or incognito window deletes what it kept when you close it.", "Clearing LiteraryWorm's site data signs you out, and books saved for offline will need saving again."]}, {"heading": "How can I control cookies on my browser?", "paragraphs": ["As the means by which you can refuse cookies through your web browser controls vary from browser to browser, you should visit your browser's help menu for more information.", "That's true of the most popular browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge and Opera. In each, you can block third-party cookies for every site, or clear the cookies and site data of one site.", "We don't use advertising networks, so there's nothing to opt out of here. If you'd like to opt out of targeted advertising elsewhere, most advertising networks offer a way to: see the Digital Advertising Alliance, the Digital Advertising Alliance of Canada or the European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance."]}, {"heading": "Local network access", "paragraphs": ["Your browser may ask whether LiteraryWorm can reach devices on your local network, such as others on your home Wi-Fi.", "Choose Block: the app never needs it, and allowing it can stop logging in from working in that browser. If you allowed it, turn it off in the site's settings (in Chrome and Edge, select the icon beside the address, then Site settings, and set Local network access to Block)."]}, {"heading": "What about other tracking technologies, like web beacons?", "paragraphs": ["Cookies are not the only way to recognize or track visitors to a website. Web beacons (sometimes called \"tracking pixels\" or \"clear gifs\") are tiny graphics files that contain a unique identifier that lets a website recognize when someone has visited it or opened an email including them.", "LiteraryWorm doesn't use web beacons or tracking pixels on the Website or in its emails. We send our emails with Mailgun's open and click tracking turned off."]}, {"heading": "Do you serve targeted advertising?", "paragraphs": ["No. We don't serve advertising on our Website, and we don't allow third parties to place cookies or web beacons on your computer or mobile device through our Website to serve or measure advertising. Google's cookies from books.google.com are set under Google's own policies; we don't use them, and we don't receive them."]}, {"heading": "How often will you update this Cookie Policy?", "paragraphs": ["We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time in order to reflect, for example, changes to the cookies we use or for other operational, legal, or regulatory reasons. Please therefore revisit this Cookie Policy regularly to stay informed about our use of cookies and related technologies.", "The Last updated date at the top of this Cookie Policy shows when it last changed. When a change matters, we'll also say so on What's new."]}, {"heading": "Where can I get further information?", "paragraphs": ["If you have any questions about our use of cookies or other technologies, please email us at support@literaryworm.com. For privacy requests, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

insert into public.changelog_entries (released_on, version, kind, title, body, major)
select '2026-11-02'::date, '2026.11', 'update', $lw$Keyword searches to try on Discover and Search$lw$, $lw$Discover and Search's start suggest a few keyword searches, such as Detective, Ghost and Friendship. Each looks through descriptions, genres and series as well as titles and authors. The Plans cards and the home page now say you can search your uploads by title, author, keywords or ISBN, even inside their text.$lw$, false
where not exists (select 1 from public.changelog_entries c where c.title = $lw$Keyword searches to try on Discover and Search$lw$ and c.version = '2026.11');
